※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4454

※ What a value of an array type is, is where its elements are, and the elements
※ of an array a function made are in that function's own room -- gone by the
※ time the caller reads them.  A slice of something that outlives the call would
※ be safe, and there is no way yet to say that one does.

fn four() → u8⟦4⟧:
    ⟦1u8, 2u8, 4u8, 8u8⟧

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    0u8
